---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { offices } from "../data/offices";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How JB Advanced Engineering Limited handles personal information, website forms, browser storage, business correspondence and privacy requests."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">JB ADVANCED ENGINEERING LIMITED</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="description">
        Your privacy matters. This policy explains how information is handled
        when you visit our website or communicate with us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section privacy-policy">
    <div class="container reading">
      <p class="privacy-date">
        Effective and last updated:{" "}
        <time datetime="2026-11-01">1 November 2026</time>
      </p>
      <p>
        JB Advanced Engineering Limited (“JBAEL”, “we”, “us” or “our”) provides
        engineering services, equipment and spares for the power generation
        industry. This policy applies to our website, company-resource access
        and business or recruitment correspondence with us. Separate contractual
        confidentiality or data-protection terms may also apply to a particular
        engagement.
      </p>

      <h2 id="information">1. Information you provide</h2>
      <p>
        Our contact, quotation, resource-access and careers forms may ask you to
        enter your name, email address, telephone number, company, project
        location, professional details, service requirements or employment
        interests. Some fields are required for the action you select.
        Supporting documents or a résumé may also be selected.
      </p>
      <p>
        Website form entries, verification answers and selected-file checks are
        processed within your browser. These forms do not transmit the entered
        information or selected files to JBAEL. Selecting a file does not upload
        it. For business enquiries, quotations or applications you wish to
        communicate directly, please use the email or telephone details on our{" "}
        <a href="/contact/">Contact Us page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you email, call or otherwise communicate directly with JBAEL, the
        information you choose to share becomes part of that correspondence.
        Please provide only information relevant to your request. Do not include
        passwords, payment-card details, government identity documents, health
        information or another person’s information unless necessary and you are
        authorised to share it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="purposes">2. How information is used</h2>
      <p>
        Information received through direct correspondence may be used to
        understand and respond to your enquiry, discuss technical requirements,
        prepare or administer quotations and services, manage supplier or
        customer relationships, and consider employment enquiries. Relevant
        correspondence may also be used to maintain business records, resolve
        disputes, prevent misuse and meet applicable legal obligations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Providing contact details for an enquiry or resource request is not a
        subscription to a marketing mailing list. You can ask us to stop
        optional promotional correspondence using the contact details below.
        Necessary responses concerning an existing request or contractual matter
        may still be required.
      </p>

      <h2 id="storage">3. Cookies, browser storage and verification</h2>
      <p>
        The website does not set advertising or analytics cookies or include
        advertising pixels or third-party analytics scripts. Fonts, images and
        downloadable company documents are served as website assets. Browser
        storage is used for the resource-access feature as described below.
      </p>
      <div class="privacy-table-wrap">
        <table class="privacy-table">
          <caption>Information used by website features</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Feature</th>
              <th scope="col">Information and purpose</th>
              <th scope="col">Duration</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Resource access</th>
              <td>
                A browser session-storage flag records that the resource form
                has been completed, so documents do not repeatedly ask for
                details. It contains no name, contact details or form answers.
              </td>
              <td>
                For the browser-tab session; browser session-restoration
                settings can affect its lifetime.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Form entries and file selection</th>
              <td>
                Values and selected-file information remain in the current page.
                Resource-form values are cleared after successful validation.
              </td>
              <td>
                Until cleared, reset or the page is left; browser autofill and
                restoration are controlled by your browser.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Captcha</th>
              <td>
                A four-letter code and your answer are checked locally to
                validate the form. No external captcha provider receives them.
              </td>
              <td>
                Until the code is refreshed, the form resets or the page is
                left.
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        You can clear website storage or manage cookies and autofill in your
        browser settings. Clearing session storage may cause the resource form
        to appear again. If storage is unavailable, resource access is
        remembered only while the current page remains open. Browser-stored
        access does not create an account or make company documents
        confidential.
      </p>

      <h2 id="technical-data">4. Technical information and website delivery</h2>
      <p>
        When you request a page, image or document, the hosting and network
        infrastructure may process technical information such as your IP
        address, requested URL, browser information and request time to deliver
        the website and support security or troubleshooting. This is separate
        from the personal information entered in forms. Infrastructure logging
        and its retention depend on the services operating the website.
      </p>

      <h2 id="sharing">5. Sharing and disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        JBAEL does not sell or rent personal information provided for business
        or recruitment correspondence. Information received by us may be shared
        with relevant personnel and, where needed, service providers supporting
        communications, business administration or an engagement. Disclosure
        should be limited to what is necessary for the relevant purpose and
        subject to appropriate confidentiality or contractual obligations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Information may also be disclosed where required by applicable law, a
        valid legal process or an authorised public authority, or where
        reasonably necessary to establish or defend legal rights or address
        fraud and security concerns.
      </p>

      <h2 id="retention">6. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Local website-form entries are not stored in a JBAEL form-submission
        database. Their browser lifetime is explained above. For information
        actually received through direct correspondence, retention depends on
        the nature of the enquiry or engagement, the need for follow-up,
        contractual and legal record-keeping requirements, and any unresolved
        disputes. You may contact us to request deletion of information we hold;
        legal or legitimate record-keeping requirements may limit what can be
        removed.
      </p>

      <h2 id="security">7. Security and confidentiality</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to handle personal information responsibly and limit its use and
        disclosure to appropriate business purposes. No website, email system or
        method of electronic storage can guarantee absolute security. Please use
        an agreed secure communication method for confidential drawings,
        commercially sensitive information or documents that require special
        protection. Never share account credentials through an enquiry.
      </p>

      <h2 id="choices">8. Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
      <p>
        You may choose not to provide optional information, clear information
        held by your browser, or contact us about information you have sent
        directly to JBAEL. Depending on applicable law, you may also request
        information about our handling of your data, access, correction or
        deletion, withdraw consent where processing relies on it, or raise a
        privacy concern.
      </p>
      <p>
        Send requests to{" "}
        <a href="mailto:info@jbepower.com">info@jbepower.com</a> with the
        subject “Privacy request”. Describe the request and the correspondence
        or interaction concerned. We may ask for information reasonably
        necessary to verify your identity or authority before disclosing or
        changing records. Requests will be assessed in accordance with
        applicable law and relevant record-keeping obligations. Where
        applicable, you may raise unresolved concerns with a competent
        regulatory authority.
      </p>

      <h2 id="external-links">
        9. External websites and communication services
      </h2>
      <p>
        Our website may link to social networks and other third-party websites.
        Email and telephone links open the communication application you choose.
        Those sites and applications operate under their own privacy terms; this
        policy does not govern their independent handling of information. Review
        their policies before sharing personal information. A link does not mean
        JBAEL controls that service.
      </p>

      <h2 id="international">10. Visitors outside India</h2>
      <p>
        JBAEL is based in India. If you communicate with us from another
        country, your correspondence may be accessed or handled in India. Where
        external hosting or communication services are involved, handling may
        also occur in the locations used by those services. Any applicable
        transfer requirements depend on the information, service and
        jurisdiction concerned.
      </p>

      <h2 id="children">11. Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This website is intended for business and professional audiences, not
        for children. We do not request children’s information for resource
        access or business enquiries. If you believe a child has provided
        personal information to us, please contact us so the matter can be
        reviewed.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy to reflect changes to information-handling
        practices, website features or applicable requirements. The current
        policy and its last-updated date will be published on this page. Where
        applicable law requires an additional notice or consent, a policy update
        alone does not replace that requirement.
      </p>

      <h2 id="privacy-contact">13. Contact us about privacy</h2>
      <address class="privacy-contact">
        <strong>JB Advanced Engineering Limited</strong>
        <br />
        {offices[0].title}
        <br />
        {offices[0].address}
        <br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@jbepower.com">info@jbepower.com</a>
        <br />
        Telephone: <a href="tel:+919136020760">+91 91360 20760</a>
      </address>
      <p>
        For other locations and general business enquiries, visit{" "}
        <a href="/contact/">Contact Us</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
